Ah, this is an interesting find. If I include the `MicroservicesModule` in the `ScheduleTaskModule`, it will run this piece of code

```typescript
  BullModule.forRootAsync({
      useFactory: async () => ({
        redis: {
          host: process.env.REDIS_HOSTNAME || 'immich_redis',
          port: 6379,
        },
      }),
    }),
```

And somehow it creates an instance of BullModule on the `server` as well. So when you put items into the queue, it will act as a worker and pull that item from the queue and start working on it as well. So it defeats the purpose of running one by one for video transcoding that we are aiming to do.

