The event listener is added each time the component mounts, but it is never removed. Svelte provides a special element that can manage window event listeners for you. An example that also prevents using the global `innerWidth` variable:

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	let innerWidth: number;

	onMount(() => {
		handleResize();
	});
</script>

<svelte:window on:resize={handleResize} bind:innerWidth />
```

Hardcoding the `md` breakpoint of 768px isn't that nice and the value might not make sense for some people without additional context. Also `@media (min-width: 768px)` means more or equal to `768` so you have an off-by-one error.

Alternatively this can probably be implemented with CSS only, using the Tailwind's `group` class. That will also prevent the layout shifting on desktop, because JS is executed later than CSS.

