It happens because Leaflet accesses `window` which isn't available for server side rendered responses. Lazy loading worked previously because a user interaction would trigger the component load, so the server never attempted to render it. But now Leaflet is loaded on a page, which means the server will attempt to load this anyway and an error is logged (the page still works though).

