Hmm I mainly dislike the `from` and `fromMany` methods, because they're pretty unusual. Besides, this code isn't directly related to the API and may as well be in it's own file. And maybe remove decorator part from the name, since it's not a decorator.

In my opinion the following approach is more idiomatic, but all good if you keep it as is:

```typescript
export class MapMarker {
	private lat: number;
	private lon: number;
	public readonly assetId?: string;

	constructor(obj: object) {
		const [lat, lon, assetId] = obj as MapMarkerResponseDto;

		this.lat = lat;
		this.lon = lon;
		this.assetId = assetId;
	}

	// Can be accessed with marker.location to make destructuring easier
	get location(): [number, number] {
		return [this.lat, this.lon];
	}
}

// markers.map(obj => new MapMarker(obj))
```

