The `ApiParams` type takes two parameters. The first one should match the `ApiFp` type which is basically a function that returns an object with functions (see example below). The second parameter is used to access a specific property of that object and will return the parameters of that function, except the last one.

Next, using [Labeled Tuple Elements](https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/release-notes/typescript-4-0.html#labeled-tuple-elements) the function definition appears as normal when you call it somewhere.


