The runtime probe runs a `MediaStore` query during object construction. This class is instantiated from `MainActivity.registerPlugins(...)` during engine setup, which is typically on the main thread; a blocking ContentProvider query here can add startup latency. Consider making the probe lazy (computed on first MediaStore access) and/or running it off the main thread with caching so plugin registration stays fast.
```suggestion
  // Probe once at first access whether _special_format is supported.
  // Officially available at S Extensions level 21+, but actual support varies across
  // devices regardless of the reported extension level -> so we probe at runtime.
  // Falls back safely if permissions aren't granted yet; after the user grants access
  // the correct projection will be picked up on the next app start.
  protected val assetProjection: Array<String> by lazy { computeAssetProjection() }

  private fun computeAssetProjection(): Array<String> {
    return if (Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= Build.VERSION_CODES.S) {
      try {
        val queryArgs = Bundle().apply { putInt(ContentResolver.QUERY_ARG_LIMIT, 1) }
        ctx.contentResolver.query(
          MediaStore.Files.getContentUri(MediaStore.VOLUME_EXTERNAL),
          arrayOf(SPECIAL_FORMAT_COLUMN),
          queryArgs,
          null
        )?.close()
        ASSET_PROJECTION
      } catch (e: Exception) {
        Log.d(TAG, "Failed to probe _special_format support, using fallback projection", e)
        ASSET_PROJECTION_FALLBACK
      }
    } else {
      ASSET_PROJECTION_FALLBACK
    }
  }
```

`ASSET_PROJECTION` is now built by `addAll(ASSET_PROJECTION_FALLBACK)`, which includes the `MediaStore.MediaColumns.XMP` blob column on Android 11+. This means on devices where `_special_format` is supported you will still project XMP for every row, which can significantly increase MediaStore query cost / CursorWindow size even though `detectPlaybackStyle` short-circuits on `_special_format`. Consider defining a separate projection for the `_special_format` path that does not include XMP, and only include XMP in the fallback projection used when `_special_format` is unavailable.
```suggestion
      // Start from the fallback projection but omit the XMP blob column to keep
      // queries lighter on devices where _special_format is supported.
      ASSET_PROJECTION_FALLBACK.forEach { column ->
        if (!(Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= Build.VERSION_CODES.R &&
              column == MediaStore.MediaColumns.XMP)
        ) {
          add(column)
        }
      }
```

